 ## Overview
-MPI Defocus Rendering synthesizes images with depth-of-field blur and lateral camera translation by compositing a precomputed Multi-Plane Image (MPI) representation [S1]. It differs from standard ray casting by operating on discrete disparity planes rather than continuous volumetric samples, allowing for efficient simulation of defocus blur via 2D image-space convolutions [S1]. It builds on [Projection and MIP Techniques](6305-projection-and-mip-techniques.md).
